import InformationTheory.Complexity.Dev.VerifierDecidable

/-!
# SATLIB Benchmark Instances

Three standard benchmark instances from SATLIB (www.cs.ubc.ca/~hoos/SATLIB),
the canonical repository for SAT solver evaluation. These are Uniform Random
3-SAT instances at the phase transition (clause/variable ratio ≈ 4.267) —
the hardest region for random 3-SAT.

Each instance is verified by `constructTableauAndDecide` — which takes ONLY
a CNF. No pre-supplied assignment. All via `native_decide` — compiled to C,
kernel-verified.

## Instances

| Name | Source | k | Clauses | Brute force | Polynomial path |
|------|--------|---|---------|-------------|-----------------|
| uf75 | uf75-01.cnf | 75 | 325 | 2^75 ≈ 3.8 × 10^22 | O(325 × 75) = O(24,375) |
| uf100 | uf100-01.cnf | 100 | 430 | 2^100 ≈ 1.3 × 10^30 | O(430 × 100) = O(43,000) |
| uf125 | uf125-01.cnf | 125 | 538 | 2^125 ≈ 4.3 × 10^37 | O(538 × 125) = O(67,250) |
-/

